  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information for the decision reason includes the outcomes and probabilities of each lottery. For Lottery A, there is one outcome (0 Euros) with 100% probability. For Lottery B, there are two outcomes (6000 Euros and -6000 Euros) each with 50% probability. Since the decision reason categorizes an outcome as probable if its probability is higher than one divided by the number of outcomes, for Lottery B, both outcomes are considered probable because 50% is higher than 1/2 or 50%. The average of probable outcomes for Lottery B is (6000 + (-6000)) / 2 = 0 Euros. For Lottery A, the average of the probable outcome is 0 Euros since there is only one outcome with 100% probability.",
